WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:02.001
-Today is Friday. Happy Friday.

00:00:02.001 --> 00:00:03.236
I hope you have a great weekend.

00:00:03.236 --> 00:00:04.503
Friday's usually when I catch up

00:00:04.503 --> 00:00:05.638
on some personal stuff,
you know,

00:00:05.638 --> 00:00:08.441
I check my inbox,
I return some emails,

00:00:08.441 --> 00:00:10.143
and, of course,
I send out thank-you notes.

00:00:10.143 --> 00:00:12.845
[ Cheering and applause ]
And I was running a bit behind.

00:00:12.845 --> 00:00:14.346
I was running a bit behind
today, so I thought,

00:00:14.346 --> 00:00:15.815
if you guys wouldn't mind,
I'd just like to write out

00:00:15.815 --> 00:00:17.350
my weekly thank-you notes
right now,

00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:18.584
if that's alright with you guys.

00:00:18.584 --> 00:00:20.419
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:20.419 --> 00:00:21.954
You guys are the best
in the biz.

00:00:21.954 --> 00:00:24.424
James, can I get some thank-you
note writing music, please?

00:00:24.424 --> 00:00:26.059
[ Playing tender tune ]
[ Laughter ]

00:00:26.059 --> 00:00:27.060
[ Applause ]

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:28.193
-Yeah.

00:00:28.193 --> 00:00:29.795
-That's a still photo.

00:00:29.795 --> 00:00:32.432
[ Laughter and cheering ]

00:00:32.432 --> 00:00:34.601
[ Laughter ]

00:00:34.601 --> 00:00:35.935
Did I tell you my new thing
I'm going to say?

00:00:35.935 --> 00:00:37.103
-No.
What's that?

00:00:37.103 --> 00:00:39.706
-You know people say,
"Oh, my God"?

00:00:39.706 --> 00:00:41.207
-Yeah.
-Or OMG.

00:00:41.207 --> 00:00:42.275
-Yeah, OMG, sure.

00:00:42.275 --> 00:00:43.509
-I just say, "OM," now.

00:00:43.509 --> 00:00:44.977
-Oh.
"Oh, my!"

00:00:44.977 --> 00:00:46.345
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:46.345 --> 00:00:48.280
-OM.
-OM!

00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:50.516
-Yeah.
-I'm going to start saying,

00:00:50.516 --> 00:00:52.485
"He figuratively..."

00:00:52.485 --> 00:00:53.686
[ Laughter ]
instead of literally.

00:00:53.686 --> 00:00:54.687
-Yeah.
-You know what I mean?

00:00:54.687 --> 00:00:56.155
People will go, "He literally

00:00:56.155 --> 00:00:57.189
blew my brains out,"

00:00:57.189 --> 00:00:58.258
you know what I mean?
Yeah.

00:00:58.258 --> 00:00:59.892
No, "he figuratively
blew my brains.

00:00:59.892 --> 00:01:01.093
It was crazy," you know?

00:01:01.093 --> 00:01:02.228
-OM.
-OM!

00:01:02.294 --> 00:01:03.362
-OM.
-Yeah.

00:01:03.362 --> 00:01:04.964
[ Laughter ]
-♪ Ohm ♪

00:01:04.964 --> 00:01:06.565
-♪ Mm ♪

00:01:06.565 --> 00:01:07.934
-OM!
-Hello.

00:01:07.934 --> 00:01:09.636
[ Laughter ]
Hi!

00:01:11.771 --> 00:01:13.139
♪♪
[ Laughter ]

00:01:13.139 --> 00:01:16.743
-Thank you, the phrase
"I'm doing my own research,"

00:01:16.743 --> 00:01:17.943
for being a fancy way of saying,

00:01:17.943 --> 00:01:19.778
"I'm checking my aunt's
Facebook wall."

00:01:19.778 --> 00:01:22.916
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:26.186 --> 00:01:27.353
♪♪
[ Laughter ]

00:01:27.353 --> 00:01:31.123
Thank you, IHOP's new
Reese's Pieces pancakes.

00:01:31.123 --> 00:01:33.359
Looks good, but should we
really be adding candy

00:01:33.359 --> 00:01:34.460
to a perfectly healthy pile

00:01:34.460 --> 00:01:35.861
of cake, butter, and syrup?

00:01:35.861 --> 00:01:38.531
[ Laughter and applause ]
-Come on, overkill.
-Come on.

00:01:41.334 --> 00:01:42.568
♪♪
[ Laughter ]

00:01:42.568 --> 00:01:44.636
Thank you,
seventh inning stretch,

00:01:44.636 --> 00:01:45.905
for correctly assuming

00:01:45.905 --> 00:01:48.273
I haven't gotten up once
in the last three hours.

00:01:48.273 --> 00:01:51.344
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:52.011 --> 00:01:53.746
-OM.
-Mm!

00:01:53.746 --> 00:01:55.147
[ Laughter ]

00:01:55.147 --> 00:01:56.615
♪♪

00:01:56.615 --> 00:02:00.553
-Thank you, pumpkin-flavored
beer coming out once a year,

00:02:00.553 --> 00:02:02.955
for being just long enough
for everyone to forget

00:02:02.955 --> 00:02:05.058
that pumpkin-flavored beer
tastes terrible.

00:02:05.058 --> 00:02:06.492
[ Laughter and applause ]
It's like, yeah,
that's why we don't --

00:02:06.492 --> 00:02:09.595
That's why this doesn't
exist all year.

00:02:09.595 --> 00:02:11.864
It's not that good.
-Zucchini-flavored beer.

00:02:11.864 --> 00:02:14.000
-Yeah, you only have
zucchini-flavored beer, right?

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:15.001
-Well, yeah, that's all I drink.

00:02:15.001 --> 00:02:17.336
I usually do zucchini, eggplant,

00:02:17.336 --> 00:02:20.239
-Oh.
-or sometimes beef.

00:02:20.239 --> 00:02:23.209
[ Laughter ]

00:02:23.275 --> 00:02:24.510
♪♪
[ Laughter ]

00:02:24.510 --> 00:02:26.346
Thank you, hay rides,

00:02:26.346 --> 00:02:28.280
for making me ask
two questions --

00:02:28.280 --> 00:02:30.549
why did we get on this
and when do we get off?

00:02:30.549 --> 00:02:32.252
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:32.252 --> 00:02:33.519
-Ah-choo!

00:02:33.519 --> 00:02:36.523
[ Laughter ]

00:02:36.523 --> 00:02:37.724
Hay ride.

00:02:37.724 --> 00:02:38.991
♪♪
[ Laughter ]

00:02:38.991 --> 00:02:40.926
-Thank you, Tums,

00:02:40.926 --> 00:02:43.495
for being sidewalk chalk
that went to med school.

00:02:43.495 --> 00:02:46.265
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:46.265 --> 00:02:47.367
They like that one.

00:02:50.270 --> 00:02:51.437
♪♪
[ Laughter ]

00:02:51.437 --> 00:02:53.406
Thank you, Frappuccinos,

00:02:53.406 --> 00:02:54.740
for answering the question,

00:02:54.740 --> 00:02:56.775
"What if a milkshake
could give you a panic attack?"

00:02:56.775 --> 00:02:58.044
[ Laughter and applause ]
There you have it, everybody.

00:02:58.044 --> 00:02:59.279
Those are my thank-you notes.

